---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import health from '../data/source-health.json';
const rows = (health as {sources?:Array<{key:string,label:string,status:string,items:number,updated_at?:string|null,age_hours?:number|null,collector?:string}>}).sources || [];
const stamp = (v?:string|null) => v && !Number.isNaN(Date.parse(v)) ? new Date(v).toLocaleString('en-GB', {dateStyle:'medium',timeStyle:'short',timeZone:'UTC'})+' UTC' : 'No successful snapshot';
const statusLabel = (s:string) => ({current:'Recent snapshot',stale:'Older than 30 hours',degraded:'Collector failed on last checked run',unavailable:'Not yet collected'} as Record<string,string>)[s] || 'Unknown';
---
<Layout title="CyberIntel | Source health and transparency" description="Publication timestamps, collector status and public-source data freshness for CyberIntel intelligence feeds.">
<section class="shell health-page">
  <header class="health-hero"><p class="health-eyebrow">TRANSPARENCY / SOURCE MONITORING</p><h1>Where the data stands.</h1><p>CyberIntel publishes periodic snapshots of public security information. These indicators describe the <strong>last validated build</strong>, not a real-time monitoring system. A source can fail between builds.</p><a class="health-link" href="https://github.com/kameshkhanna/cyberintel/actions/workflows/update-intel.yml" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Review collection workflow and failures ↗</a></header>
  <div class="health-top"><div><small>OVERALL PUBLISHED SNAPSHOT</small><strong>{health.overall === 'current' ? 'Current at validation' : health.overall === 'degraded' ? 'Attention required' : 'Not yet checked'}</strong></div><div><small>HEALTH REPORT GENERATED</small><strong>{stamp(health.generated_at)}</strong></div></div>
  <div class="health-list">
  {rows.length ? rows.map(s => <article class="health-row"><div><span class={`health-dot ${s.status}`} aria-hidden="true"></span><h2>{s.label}</h2><p>{statusLabel(s.status)}</p></div><dl><div><dt>Records shown</dt><dd>{s.items}</dd></div><div><dt>Source refreshed</dt><dd>{stamp(s.updated_at)}</dd></div><div><dt>Age at validation</dt><dd>{s.age_hours == null ? 'Unknown' : `${s.age_hours} hours`}</dd></div></dl></article>) : <div class="health-empty">No validation report published yet. The scheduled GitHub Action generates this report when data collection runs successfully enough to pass validation.</div>}
  </div>
  <div class="health-notes"><h2>How to interpret these indicators</h2><p>“Recent snapshot” means the data timestamp was within 30 hours at the time of validation. It does not mean the source has been checked right now. Partial collector failures are disclosed; older cached items may remain published. All data and third-party content are untrusted until reviewed against the original source.</p><p>CyberIntel does not store your organisation’s assets or execute KQL, SPL or YARA rules on behalf of visitors. If a published link or security statement appears suspicious, please report it using the repository's security contact process.</p><a href="/methodology/">Read collection methodology ↗</a></div>
</section>
</Layout>
<style>
.health-page{padding-top:70px;padding-bottom:90px}.health-hero{max-width:790px}.health-eyebrow{font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.11em;color:#72715f}.health-hero h1{font-size:clamp(42px,5vw,76px);line-height:1.08;margin:18px 0}.health-hero p{font-size:18px;line-height:1.8;max-width:730px}.health-link{display:inline-block;margin-top:14px;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:5px}.health-top{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px;margin:48px 0 20px}.health-top>div{padding:25px 28px;border:1px solid #ddd8ce;border-radius:16px;background:#f5f2ec;display:grid;gap:11px}.health-top small,.health-row dt{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.09em;color:#666}.health-top strong{font-size:23px}.health-list{border-top:1px solid #ddd8ce}.health-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(230px,1fr) minmax(0,1.4fr);gap:25px;padding:28px 6px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd8ce}.health-row h2{font-size:23px;margin:0}.health-row p{font-size:13px;margin:9px 0 0;color:#696969}.health-dot{width:9px;height:9px;background:#a0998d;border-radius:100%;display:inline-block;margin-bottom:11px}.health-dot.current{background:#26785e}.health-dot.stale,.health-dot.degraded{background:#bf8338}.health-row dl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:20px;margin:0;align-items:center}.health-row dt{text-transform:uppercase}.health-row dd{margin:7px 0 0;font-size:14px;font-weight:650}.health-empty{padding:40px 0}.health-notes{max-width:800px;margin-top:55px}.health-notes h2{font-size:26px}.health-notes p{line-height:1.8;color:#515151}.health-notes a{text-decoration:underline}@media(max-width:750px){.health-row{grid-template-columns:1fr}.health-row dl{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.health-top{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
